Cosmian KMS — license notice and planned removal
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The deployment includes Cosmian KMS (ghcr.io/cosmian/kms, Copyright Cosmian
Tech SAS). It is licensed under the Business Source License 1.1 (BUSL-1.1),
NOT under an open-source license. It is not covered by the Apache License of
this project. Its Additional Use Grant permits production use only up to
2 vCPUs (or 1 physical core) and does not permit offering the Licensed Work
to third parties. Each version changes to MPL-2.0 four years after its
publication. See https://github.com/Cosmian/kms/blob/main/LICENSE.

Cosmian KMS is an excellent product, and we thank its authors. But its
license restrictions harm a non-profit project like iotgw-ng: they prevent
users from freely running, scaling and sharing the platform. For this reason
Cosmian KMS will be REMOVED from this project soon and replaced by an
open-source key-management service. Until then, anyone who deploys iotgw-ng
is responsible for complying with the Cosmian KMS license.

